1
00:01:41,789 --> 00:01:48,970
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:51,720
[Episode 13]

3
00:02:09,470 --> 00:02:10,000
Who is it?

4
00:02:10,910 --> 00:02:12,440
Shen Fuxuan, are you awake?

5
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:14,710
Yes.

6
00:02:21,079 --> 00:02:21,750
Coming.

7
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,310
Morning.

8
00:02:25,310 --> 00:02:26,570
Did you get this for me?

9
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:27,800
Thank you.

10
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:29,750
Well,

11
00:02:30,360 --> 00:02:32,760
I got this last night
in case you got hungry.

12
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:35,470
Morning.

13
00:02:38,160 --> 00:02:39,280
Why are you here?

14
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:41,040
Surprising, right?

15
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:43,910
You two wait here for a bit.

16
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:45,079
I'll go change my clothes,

17
00:02:45,079 --> 00:02:47,680
and then we can go down
for breakfast together.

18
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:10,560
I don't think you should drink coffee
on an empty stomach.

19
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,690
I need to drink some.

20
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,120
I didn't dare to sleep last night,

21
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,120
so I'm afraid I'll get sleepy later.

22
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:16,400
Thanks to you,

23
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:18,160
I slept very well last night.

24
00:03:18,840 --> 00:03:19,630
Thank you.

25
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:30,820
You didn't sleep well last night either?

26
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:34,079
I'm not used to unfamiliar beds.

27
00:03:39,870 --> 00:03:41,280
It's time. I have to go.

28
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:45,320
I'll attend your presentation.

29
00:03:45,710 --> 00:03:46,430
Really?

30
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:47,590
Of course.

31
00:03:49,910 --> 00:03:51,100
It's such an important occasion.

32
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,360
How could I miss it?

33
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:57,930
See you later then.

34
00:03:58,030 --> 00:03:58,840
See you later.

35
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:01,030
See you later, Shen Fuxuan.

36
00:04:01,030 --> 00:04:01,840
See you later.

37
00:04:18,899 --> 00:04:22,790
[The 6th Nanhai Provincial Symposium
on Marine Science Development]

38
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:24,480
Okay, thank you.

39
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,070
Today,

40
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:28,480
we have a special segment.

41
00:04:28,750 --> 00:04:30,800
We've invited a high school student

42
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:32,240
to interpret and discuss

43
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:34,950
marine issues from her perspective.

44
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,000
Please welcome

45
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,070
Lin Zhixia, a high school student
from Nanhai No. 1 High School.

46
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:40,670
A round of applause, please.

47
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:45,110
[The 6th Nanhai Provincial Symposium
on Marine Science Development]

48
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,080
[The 6th Nanhai Provincial Symposium
on Marine Science Development]

49
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,720
Hello, everyone.

50
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:08,190
I'm the high school student
representative today, Lin Zhixia.

51
00:05:08,190 --> 00:05:10,160
I was very nervous backstage just now.

52
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:12,190
Seeing so many outstanding experts
and scholars

53
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:14,120
engaging in in-depth discussions

54
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:16,120
made me, as a student, realize that

55
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,520
the academic path
is a long and arduous one.

56
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:21,240
Today I want to share with you

57
00:05:21,240 --> 00:05:22,680
a topic that is closely related to us.

58
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,510
Don't take photos. You'll distract her.

59
00:05:24,510 --> 00:05:25,630
What do you know?

60
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:27,110
I've turned off the flash.

61
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:29,220
I'm recording her highlight moment.

62
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,170
Point it up a bit.

63
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:33,430
It has already attracted
widespread attention.

64
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:36,630
But today I want to specifically
discuss microplastics.

65
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:41,720
There is currently
no unified definition of microplastics.

66
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,360
They generally refer to
plastic fragments at the millimeter

67
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,390
or even micrometer level.

68
00:05:45,830 --> 00:05:48,090
Actually, this topic is quite advanced.

69
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:50,740
What.

70
00:05:51,800 --> 00:05:53,130
What do you mean by that?

71
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:55,690
I'm afraid you won't understand it.

72
00:05:55,690 --> 00:05:57,740
Actually, you can go home
and brush up on the basics.

73
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:59,000
Don't force yourself.

74
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,180
When have you scored better than me
on an exam this semester?

75
00:06:03,180 --> 00:06:05,440
If anyone doesn't understand, it's you.

76
00:06:06,280 --> 00:06:08,140
This is a Marine Science Seminar.

77
00:06:08,430 --> 00:06:09,600
Have you forgotten who my mom is?

78
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,700
I've been immersed in it since childhood.

79
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:13,000
Even my bedtime stories
were about oceanography.

80
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,950
Thus, they enter the food chain.

81
00:06:15,190 --> 00:06:17,870
This causes problems for the creatures,
including indigestion, energy deficiency,

82
00:06:17,870 --> 00:06:20,040
injury, poisoning, and even death.

83
00:06:21,270 --> 00:06:22,470
As we just mentioned,

84
00:06:22,480 --> 00:06:25,480
microplastics enter the ocean
through various pathways.

85
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,920
Now let's see what those pathways are.

86
00:06:30,270 --> 00:06:32,390
There are 4 main pathways of input.

87
00:06:32,870 --> 00:06:34,000
Lifestyle pathway.

88
00:06:34,159 --> 00:06:35,920
Our daily domestic wastewater

89
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,870
will all be discharged into the ocean.

90
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:39,200
Laundry wastewater...

91
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:18,370
[The Harm of Microplastics
to the Nanhai Ecosystem]

92
00:07:26,920 --> 00:07:29,130
[The Harm of Microplastics
to the Nanhai Ecosystem]

93
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,120
Fourth, and most importantly,

94
00:07:31,120 --> 00:07:32,950
is to raise public awareness.

95
00:07:37,610 --> 00:07:42,350
[Thanks]

96
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:42,510
Due to a lack of systematic study
in oceanography,

97
00:07:42,510 --> 00:07:43,190
my research

98
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:45,390
remains at a relatively superficial stage.

99
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:47,070
I would like to express my special thanks

100
00:07:47,070 --> 00:07:48,890
to Professor Shen Zhaohua's lab team

101
00:07:48,890 --> 00:07:50,560
for their patient guidance.

102
00:07:50,650 --> 00:07:52,120
With their help,

103
00:07:52,159 --> 00:07:53,430
I was able to collect seawater samples

104
00:07:53,430 --> 00:07:55,850
and offshore sediments
of Nanhai Province shores,

105
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:57,190
and more effectively observe

106
00:07:57,190 --> 00:08:00,450
the distribution and
pollution status of microplastics.

107
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:02,430
I think in the next decade,

108
00:08:02,630 --> 00:08:04,160
microplastics are very likely to become

109
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:06,960
one of the biggest challenges
in global ocean governance.

110
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:09,040
I hope the treatment
and prevention of microplastics

111
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,240
will become an issue that everyone
pays more attention to.

112
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,560
I also hope my sharing

113
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:14,850
can provide you with some new ideas.

114
00:08:14,880 --> 00:08:16,720
That concludes my presentation for today.

115
00:08:16,720 --> 00:08:17,630
Thank you all.

116
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:48,440
Later, make a copy of your slides today

117
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,150
for Ms. Guan.

118
00:08:58,930 --> 00:09:00,420
Great. So excellent.

119
00:09:00,450 --> 00:09:01,530
When she was still young,

120
00:09:01,530 --> 00:09:02,840
I met her at the aquarium.

121
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:04,670
So she is really a gifted talent.

122
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:05,880
The reason I invited her

123
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,880
is that our team needs such a talent.

124
00:09:08,510 --> 00:09:10,100
Xia, Ms. Guan here is

125
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:11,440
a prominent teacher in the field

126
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:13,100
with her own unique insights on the

127
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:15,300
future development of marine science.

128
00:09:46,410 --> 00:09:47,370
I'm back.

129
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:53,520
Baihui, come here.

130
00:09:58,140 --> 00:10:00,720
[Gentle Battle Hymn]

131
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:05,170
Explain this.

132
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:08,870
This... This...

133
00:10:08,890 --> 00:10:11,700
I've noticed you haven't been as quick
to get up these past couple of days.

134
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,980
I thought you had
finally figured things out

135
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:14,580
and stayed up late studying.

136
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,410
Turns out you were reading this.

137
00:10:16,410 --> 00:10:17,810
Where did this come from?

138
00:10:19,580 --> 00:10:20,290
Did you buy it yourself?

139
00:10:20,290 --> 00:10:20,980
No.

140
00:10:23,410 --> 00:10:23,870
This...

141
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,110
[Gentle Battle Hymn]

142
00:10:24,370 --> 00:10:25,630
This is just...

143
00:10:27,820 --> 00:10:30,500
a gift from Lin Zhixia.

144
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:32,070
but I didn't read it.

145
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:34,050
A gift from Lin Zhixia?

146
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:36,860
Do ace students have time to read this?

147
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:38,580
They are all busy
doing practice questions.

148
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:39,980
She knows that for this exam,

149
00:10:39,980 --> 00:10:41,250
your grades dropped so severely,

150
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:42,980
yet she still gave you this leisure book?

151
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:45,900
She is mocking you
for never being able to catch up to her!

152
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:48,620
Baihui, we wouldn't hurt you.

153
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:50,270
She has good grades.

154
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:52,220
She's pretending to be your good friend

155
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:54,100
to make you lower your guard.

156
00:10:54,120 --> 00:10:56,120
And you actually took it seriously.

157
00:11:02,570 --> 00:11:03,650
[Gentle Battle Hymn]

158
00:11:23,170 --> 00:11:24,890
Go, return it to her today.

159
00:11:25,770 --> 00:11:28,340
Dad, I swear I haven't read it.

160
00:11:28,340 --> 00:11:29,650
I will never talk to her again.

161
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:30,580
As for this book,

162
00:11:31,130 --> 00:11:32,610
can I just throw it away myself?

163
00:11:32,610 --> 00:11:34,140
I'll pretend I never had it.

164
00:11:35,310 --> 00:11:37,600
If you won't go, I will.

165
00:11:37,700 --> 00:11:39,430
I will personally hand this book to her

166
00:11:39,430 --> 00:11:40,580
and let her reflect on

167
00:11:40,580 --> 00:11:41,580
her true intentions.

168
00:11:41,580 --> 00:11:43,220
Mom, if I really do it,

169
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:45,620
-what will my classmates think of me?
-Is that important?

170
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,250
Classmates are just competitors.

171
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:48,340
When Lin Zhixia gave you the book,

172
00:11:48,340 --> 00:11:49,740
she was probably mocking you in her heart.

173
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:50,800
Do you understand?

174
00:11:51,370 --> 00:11:52,130
But Dad...

175
00:11:52,130 --> 00:11:53,990
I'm not discussing this with you.

176
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:02,740
I got it.

177
00:12:26,200 --> 00:12:27,130
You took photos?

178
00:12:32,340 --> 00:12:33,100
Let me see.

179
00:12:45,740 --> 00:12:46,740
Videos, too.

180
00:13:11,100 --> 00:13:12,340
You took so many.

181
00:13:15,120 --> 00:13:16,500
How did I do?

182
00:13:17,290 --> 00:13:18,010
Good.

183
00:13:18,290 --> 00:13:19,250
Really good.

184
00:13:36,250 --> 00:13:38,380
What do you think of my research topic?

185
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:39,500
Good.

186
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:40,770
Very good.

187
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:51,620
A strawberry!

188
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:54,120
These are all your favorites.

189
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:58,500
We sat through a morning of reports.

190
00:13:58,500 --> 00:13:59,900
Haven't you seen enough?

191
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:02,500
Eat something.

192
00:14:02,670 --> 00:14:03,650
You must be hungry.

193
00:14:03,650 --> 00:14:04,280
Eat up.

194
00:14:09,170 --> 00:14:09,770
By the way.

195
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:11,980
My mom still has wrap-up work
this afternoon,

196
00:14:11,980 --> 00:14:13,110
so we have free time.

197
00:14:13,500 --> 00:14:15,300
Is there anything you want to do?

198
00:14:19,890 --> 00:14:21,700
A sci-fi blockbuster
was released recently.

199
00:14:21,700 --> 00:14:23,100
Let's go watch the movie.

200
00:14:23,220 --> 00:14:23,940
Sure.

201
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:34,550
Where's my share?

202
00:14:36,340 --> 00:14:37,340
Go help yourself.

203
00:14:54,530 --> 00:14:56,360
[Currently Airing]

204
00:14:56,360 --> 00:15:01,740
[Snacks Ordering]

205
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:01,290
Hello. How can I help you?

206
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:08,820
These badges are so beautiful.

207
00:15:08,860 --> 00:15:11,200
These are badges
for the movie "Pale Blue Dot."

208
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:13,030
Our cinema is having
a promotion right now.

209
00:15:13,030 --> 00:15:13,980
If you participate,

210
00:15:13,980 --> 00:15:15,710
you can check in and get a badge.

211
00:15:16,460 --> 00:15:17,390
What promotion?

212
00:15:17,390 --> 00:15:18,050
Right here.

213
00:15:18,530 --> 00:15:19,790
This is the promotion.

214
00:15:20,250 --> 00:15:22,910
[Exclusive Benefit for Couples]

215
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:24,760
Couples can take a photo together
to get a limited-edition badge.

216
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:32,810
[Capture the moment of love]

217
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:34,910
This is the couples' photo check-in wall.

218
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,390
[Capture the moment of love]

219
00:15:41,320 --> 00:15:43,120
Non-couples should be fine too.

220
00:15:43,340 --> 00:15:45,460
Why don't we take a photo together?

221
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:46,430
[Winter Snow]

222
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:47,270
We should be able to get the badge too.

223
00:15:47,270 --> 00:15:48,000
Makes sense.

224
00:15:50,410 --> 00:15:51,850
I don't think that's a good idea.

225
00:15:51,850 --> 00:15:54,560
[Capture the moment of love]

226
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:54,620
What's wrong with it?

227
00:15:54,620 --> 00:15:55,680
Please. Thank you.

228
00:15:56,050 --> 00:15:57,780
You two, stand a little closer.

229
00:15:58,500 --> 00:15:59,300
Strike a pose.

230
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:01,050
Let's do a peace sign.

231
00:16:01,050 --> 00:16:02,080
I'm going to take the picture now.

232
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:02,600
Ready.

233
00:16:02,740 --> 00:16:05,650
Three, two, one.

234
00:16:18,230 --> 00:16:22,190
[Exclusively for couples]

235
00:16:18,790 --> 00:16:21,450
Here is the photo of you two.
Please keep it safe.

236
00:16:26,050 --> 00:16:27,980
This photo is really interesting.

237
00:16:28,580 --> 00:16:29,580
Can I keep it?

238
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,600
I want this badge.

239
00:16:38,740 --> 00:16:39,550
Here you go.

240
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:43,000
Thank you.

241
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:43,930
You're welcome.

242
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:50,340
Row 5, seats 9, 10, and 11.

243
00:16:52,290 --> 00:16:52,950
Right here.

244
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:55,670
I'll go in first.

245
00:16:57,290 --> 00:16:58,100
Move inside.

246
00:17:12,550 --> 00:17:15,150
It's been a long time
since I came to the cinema.

247
00:18:13,710 --> 00:18:14,720
Shen Fuxuan.

248
00:18:15,980 --> 00:18:17,040
Hold out your hand.

249
00:18:19,470 --> 00:18:20,270
Both hands.

250
00:18:21,010 --> 00:18:21,850
Both.

251
00:18:22,500 --> 00:18:23,440
Both hands.

252
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:32,760
It's more convenient to hold it
and eat it yourself.

253
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,010
Is it enough?

254
00:19:21,050 --> 00:19:21,850
Jin Baihui?

255
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:29,090
I'm Lin Zhixia's brother.

256
00:19:29,610 --> 00:19:30,500
My name is Lin Zeqiu.

257
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,220
Hello.

258
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:31,940
Hello.

259
00:19:32,570 --> 00:19:33,930
How do you know who I am?

260
00:19:34,900 --> 00:19:37,500
You are one of the top students
in my sister's class.

261
00:19:37,500 --> 00:19:38,330
I know you.

262
00:19:38,770 --> 00:19:40,280
And after the school anniversary,

263
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,210
who in the school doesn't know you?

264
00:19:45,810 --> 00:19:47,810
Are you here to see my sister today?

265
00:19:50,380 --> 00:19:50,980
I...

266
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:00,290
This...

267
00:20:01,250 --> 00:20:02,980
Please give this to Lin Zhixia.

268
00:20:10,290 --> 00:20:13,180
She's not at home. Maybe wait a bit?

269
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:25,240
We are all stardust.

270
00:20:26,270 --> 00:20:28,740
Adrift in the same darkness.

271
00:20:30,550 --> 00:20:31,810
Even when we're apart,

272
00:20:32,940 --> 00:20:35,110
we are still under the same sky.

273
00:20:35,740 --> 00:20:37,370
We don't own each other,

274
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:40,530
but we can light up
one another's darkness.

275
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:48,960
I'm going to the restroom.

276
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,200
Are you cold?

277
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:38,570
This is hot.

278
00:22:39,030 --> 00:22:40,030
Hold it to warm up.

279
00:22:41,030 --> 00:22:41,630
Thank you.

280
00:22:41,960 --> 00:22:42,620
No problem.

281
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:51,720
You haven't been here, have you?

282
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,570
This is Lin Zhixia's and my secret base.

283
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,460
She loves drawing.

284
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:03,900
This is a drawing of our house
from when she was little.

285
00:23:04,590 --> 00:23:06,240
She drew it in kindergarten.

286
00:23:07,210 --> 00:23:09,220
No, in primary school.

287
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:13,960
That one over there
is from kindergarten.

288
00:23:14,110 --> 00:23:14,900
And this one.

289
00:23:15,510 --> 00:23:16,140
This was

290
00:23:16,680 --> 00:23:18,290
also drawn in kindergarten.

291
00:23:19,750 --> 00:23:22,550
Her drawings were cuter back then.

292
00:23:23,190 --> 00:23:25,900
And these are from middle school.

293
00:23:25,960 --> 00:23:27,360
These are less childish.

294
00:23:27,470 --> 00:23:28,260
She said

295
00:23:28,280 --> 00:23:29,920
I was that little frog,

296
00:23:30,500 --> 00:23:33,560
and she'd be the umbrella to shelter me
when she grew up.

297
00:23:34,680 --> 00:23:36,060
Give me a break.

298
00:23:36,350 --> 00:23:38,210
Who knows who's protecting whom?

299
00:23:39,200 --> 00:23:39,930
Look at this.

300
00:23:41,300 --> 00:23:43,420
This is a seat from a minibus.

301
00:23:44,610 --> 00:23:47,750
We snatched it from a junk collector.

302
00:23:49,640 --> 00:23:50,900
It's actually broken.

303
00:23:51,480 --> 00:23:53,140
See, it has no leg on that side.

304
00:23:53,180 --> 00:23:54,090
See, we stacked bricks there

305
00:23:54,090 --> 00:23:55,950
to keep it steady and functional.

306
00:23:56,330 --> 00:23:57,250
Just like that.

307
00:23:57,690 --> 00:23:59,550
Here, there are bricks here, too.

308
00:23:59,820 --> 00:24:01,160
This one is broken too,

309
00:24:01,380 --> 00:24:03,240
but it works with bricks under it.

310
00:24:04,300 --> 00:24:05,830
My parents' supermarket had

311
00:24:05,830 --> 00:24:08,030
old vegetable crates. We put them here,

312
00:24:08,160 --> 00:24:11,290
threw a cloth over them,
and it became our space capsule.

313
00:24:12,530 --> 00:24:13,660
As for this cloth...

314
00:24:14,510 --> 00:24:16,420
I used it when I was little.

315
00:24:16,450 --> 00:24:17,720
It was my blanket.

316
00:24:19,210 --> 00:24:20,210
And there's more.

317
00:24:20,570 --> 00:24:22,050
The navigator sits here,

318
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:24,160
and there's an accelerator inside.

319
00:24:26,750 --> 00:24:29,030
It's nice having siblings.

320
00:24:30,550 --> 00:24:31,770
It was all her idea.

321
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:33,970
I just did what she said.

322
00:24:39,380 --> 00:24:40,610
But I like it here too.

323
00:24:42,310 --> 00:24:44,790
Because here you can see

324
00:24:45,310 --> 00:24:46,680
the whole sky.

325
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:57,800
That's the Winter Triangle.

326
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:00,120
Next to it is the Hexagon.

327
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:02,260
It's very visible.

328
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:06,530
Among them, Sirius, the closest one to us,

329
00:25:06,940 --> 00:25:08,400
is slowly approaching us.

330
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:14,780
Are you interested in astronomy?

331
00:25:16,140 --> 00:25:18,940
I'm the president of
the school's astronomy club.

332
00:25:19,870 --> 00:25:21,200
Aren't you in any clubs?

333
00:25:22,350 --> 00:25:25,440
No. I'm afraid it'll affect my studies.

334
00:25:27,480 --> 00:25:28,680
Not really.

335
00:25:28,680 --> 00:25:30,540
You just need to manage your time.

336
00:25:31,570 --> 00:25:34,430
You can come check out
the astronomy club sometime.

337
00:25:34,680 --> 00:25:35,460
Besides,

338
00:25:36,030 --> 00:25:38,390
if you study all day,

339
00:25:38,530 --> 00:25:39,730
won't you go crazy?

340
00:25:51,880 --> 00:25:53,340
The movie was really good.

341
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:55,200
Pale Blue Dot.

342
00:25:55,750 --> 00:25:57,350
The blue dot is our Earth.

343
00:25:57,680 --> 00:25:58,960
Alone in the universe,

344
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:00,620
yet afraid of not being alone.

345
00:26:01,790 --> 00:26:02,850
It really was good.

346
00:26:04,070 --> 00:26:06,130
Were you actually paying attention?

347
00:26:10,830 --> 00:26:11,590
Hello, Mom.

348
00:26:13,750 --> 00:26:14,480
Okay.

349
00:26:15,070 --> 00:26:15,830
Got it.

350
00:26:18,770 --> 00:26:19,790
My mom is done over there.

351
00:26:19,790 --> 00:26:20,850
I need to head over.

352
00:26:21,830 --> 00:26:22,610
Do you want to...

353
00:26:22,610 --> 00:26:23,480
Go ahead.

354
00:26:23,880 --> 00:26:24,940
I'll take her home.

355
00:26:31,100 --> 00:26:32,070
Alright then.

356
00:26:32,340 --> 00:26:33,400
It's getting late.

357
00:26:33,960 --> 00:26:35,220
It's not safe outside.

358
00:26:36,680 --> 00:26:37,940
Go back and rest early.

359
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:40,200
Let's go.

360
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,070
Help me hold my bag.

361
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:01,200
Is this book...

362
00:27:05,350 --> 00:27:07,830
Lin Zhixia gave this to me.

363
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:10,160
My parents found out.

364
00:27:11,070 --> 00:27:13,670
They were afraid
it would affect my studies...

365
00:27:16,840 --> 00:27:18,440
So they asked me to return it.

366
00:27:25,440 --> 00:27:26,550
It's already torn like this.

367
00:27:26,550 --> 00:27:29,480
Why didn't you just throw it
in a trash can by the road?

368
00:27:32,350 --> 00:27:33,400
You're so honest,

369
00:27:33,790 --> 00:27:34,680
so naive.

370
00:27:37,350 --> 00:27:38,160
That's true.

371
00:27:45,590 --> 00:27:47,120
Alright then, give it to me.

372
00:27:50,950 --> 00:27:51,810
I'll handle it.

373
00:27:53,550 --> 00:27:55,610
Just say you've already returned it.

374
00:27:59,640 --> 00:28:00,400
Thank you.

375
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:08,300
I guess I'm already used to it.

376
00:28:09,160 --> 00:28:11,160
I do whatever they tell me.

377
00:28:14,510 --> 00:28:17,240
Please say sorry to Lin Zhixia for me.

378
00:28:25,400 --> 00:28:27,060
She actually won't blame you.

379
00:28:31,880 --> 00:28:35,070
My sister didn't have many friends
when she was little.

380
00:28:36,210 --> 00:28:39,620
She was quite a misfit.

381
00:28:40,880 --> 00:28:41,750
So my parents

382
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:45,930
were also very worried
about her making friends.

383
00:28:47,750 --> 00:28:49,160
If they knew you were coming today,

384
00:28:49,160 --> 00:28:50,960
they would have been very happy.

385
00:28:53,160 --> 00:28:53,880
I...

386
00:28:56,070 --> 00:28:58,400
I'm not sure if we're considered friends.

387
00:28:59,070 --> 00:29:00,270
She gave you a book,

388
00:29:00,400 --> 00:29:02,260
so you are definitely her friend.

389
00:29:08,750 --> 00:29:11,440
I think Lin Zhixia
is genuinely nice to me,

390
00:29:12,030 --> 00:29:13,960
but my parents always believe that

391
00:29:14,110 --> 00:29:17,370
she is purposely distracting me
with singing and leisure books.

392
00:29:17,370 --> 00:29:19,720
She's afraid I'd surpass her.

393
00:29:21,510 --> 00:29:24,440
Your parents are overthinking.
That's impossible.

394
00:29:26,960 --> 00:29:30,180
I'm not saying it's impossible
for you to surpass her.

395
00:29:30,830 --> 00:29:31,930
I mean...

396
00:29:32,400 --> 00:29:35,430
In this regard, my sister...

397
00:29:36,300 --> 00:29:37,920
Her brain, you know,

398
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:40,590
is just a bit abnormal.

399
00:29:48,790 --> 00:29:50,450
But when she gave you the book,

400
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:52,620
it must have been sincere.

401
00:30:09,900 --> 00:30:13,630
When I was a kid, I loved watching
the stars with my brother the most.

402
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,170
Jiang Yubai, look.

403
00:30:15,710 --> 00:30:18,000
There are so many stars
in the sky tonight.

404
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:18,590
Yeah.

405
00:30:21,480 --> 00:30:23,830
Are you also looking at Sirius?

406
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:25,870
How did you know?

407
00:30:26,350 --> 00:30:27,770
Because the aliens in the movie

408
00:30:27,770 --> 00:30:29,090
were from Sirius.

409
00:30:31,750 --> 00:30:33,070
If you were given a chance

410
00:30:33,070 --> 00:30:35,110
to explore outer space for aliens,

411
00:30:35,590 --> 00:30:37,240
but you probably wouldn't be
able to come back,

412
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,070
would you go?

413
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:41,550
In life,

414
00:30:41,640 --> 00:30:43,200
people are naturally curious.

415
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:45,800
We all want to see
what the universe looks like.

416
00:30:46,550 --> 00:30:48,080
But if I couldn't come back,

417
00:30:49,640 --> 00:30:50,550
I'd probably have too many

418
00:30:50,550 --> 00:30:52,350
emotional ties I can't let go of.

419
00:30:52,830 --> 00:30:53,750
I would go.

420
00:30:54,830 --> 00:30:56,240
Even if you can't come back?

421
00:30:56,240 --> 00:30:57,640
I don't need to come back.

422
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,420
Once I find a new home,

423
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:01,240
all humanity can just move over.

424
00:32:07,210 --> 00:32:08,100
Then you...

425
00:32:08,130 --> 00:32:08,860
I'm not cold.

426
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:19,350
Did you know?

427
00:32:20,030 --> 00:32:22,880
Sirius is actually 8.6 light-years
away from us.

428
00:32:25,240 --> 00:32:27,980
Because its brightness
is 25 times that of the Sun,

429
00:32:27,980 --> 00:32:30,160
we can see it

430
00:32:30,180 --> 00:32:31,110
from so far away.

431
00:32:33,030 --> 00:32:33,680
This beam of light

432
00:32:33,680 --> 00:32:36,030
took 8.6 years to reach Earth.

433
00:32:36,920 --> 00:32:38,590
That means before we even met,

434
00:32:39,070 --> 00:32:40,310
it had already embarked

435
00:32:40,310 --> 00:32:41,960
on the journey to meet us.

436
00:32:51,310 --> 00:32:52,110
How romantic.

437
00:32:54,310 --> 00:32:55,400
Since

438
00:32:56,110 --> 00:32:58,110
it had such a hard time getting here,

439
00:32:58,330 --> 00:33:01,720
shall we take a photo with it
as a souvenir?

440
00:33:02,900 --> 00:33:03,710
Sure.

441
00:33:13,330 --> 00:33:14,570
It's right here.

442
00:33:14,600 --> 00:33:16,880
Ready, 3, 2, 1.

443
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:20,960
It's a bit crooked.

444
00:33:21,080 --> 00:33:22,410
Let's take another one.

445
00:33:22,780 --> 00:33:25,010
Three, two, one.

446
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:27,740
It's a bit blurry and out of focus.

447
00:33:28,640 --> 00:33:29,440
Let's take another one.

448
00:33:29,440 --> 00:33:30,770
Three, two, one.

449
00:33:33,130 --> 00:33:36,100
[Happiness is so simple]

450
00:33:33,660 --> 00:33:35,260
This one is a bit out of focus.

451
00:33:35,420 --> 00:33:36,750
Let's take another one.

452
00:33:37,720 --> 00:33:38,220
Three.

453
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:39,800
The bus is here.

454
00:34:05,200 --> 00:34:07,750
Many of the photos we just took
are out of focus.

455
00:34:07,750 --> 00:34:09,810
Should we retake...

456
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:14,340
♪ The moment our eyes met,
my world came alive with color ♪

457
00:34:15,010 --> 00:34:19,380
♪ Could this be how love begins? ♪

458
00:34:19,900 --> 00:34:22,880
♪ These unspoken feelings
are so hard to figure out ♪

459
00:34:23,460 --> 00:34:28,860
♪ Hidden deep within your gaze ♪

460
00:34:29,179 --> 00:34:33,610
♪ Sometimes, I imagine
drifting beyond the skies with you ♪

461
00:34:34,159 --> 00:34:38,570
♪ Shimmering light
dances over the flower in bloom ♪

462
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:42,179
♪ After all we've been through,
our fates remain intertwined ♪

463
00:34:42,750 --> 00:34:49,540
♪ Perhaps fate favors me now ♪

464
00:35:34,170 --> 00:35:35,500
Thank you, Jiang Yubai.

465
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:36,550
I'm home.

466
00:35:37,610 --> 00:35:38,440
Then...

467
00:35:40,170 --> 00:35:41,700
See you at school next week.

468
00:35:56,760 --> 00:35:57,440
Here you go.

469
00:36:04,070 --> 00:36:05,470
Good night, Jiang Yubai.

470
00:36:06,440 --> 00:36:08,840
Good night, Lin Zhixia.

471
00:36:52,860 --> 00:36:53,670
Lin Zhixia!

472
00:36:55,990 --> 00:36:56,790
Come here!

473
00:36:58,040 --> 00:36:59,090
What's wrong?

474
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:00,850
Where did you go?

475
00:37:01,110 --> 00:37:01,710
I...

476
00:37:01,710 --> 00:37:03,440
I called your hotel twice.

477
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:04,590
They said you checked out this afternoon.

478
00:37:04,590 --> 00:37:06,590
Where did you go?
Why are you back so late?

479
00:37:06,590 --> 00:37:09,190
If you were 10 minutes later,
I would have called the police!

480
00:37:09,190 --> 00:37:10,480
The seminar was in the suburbs.

481
00:37:10,480 --> 00:37:11,800
It takes time for me to get back.

482
00:37:11,800 --> 00:37:12,630
You knew it would take time,

483
00:37:12,630 --> 00:37:14,160
so why didn't you call home?

484
00:37:15,190 --> 00:37:17,720
How could I call
when I don't even have a phone?

485
00:37:21,000 --> 00:37:21,550
Well...

486
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:26,530
Then you need to get a phone.

487
00:37:40,110 --> 00:37:41,370
Mom, Dad, you're back.

488
00:37:41,710 --> 00:37:42,360
You...

489
00:37:42,360 --> 00:37:43,820
Why aren't you asleep yet?

490
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:45,600
What are you two up to?

491
00:37:49,150 --> 00:37:51,150
We were waiting for you to come back.

492
00:37:54,710 --> 00:37:55,840
Is something wrong?

493
00:37:57,140 --> 00:37:58,570
Just drop it.

494
00:37:59,030 --> 00:37:59,990
No.

495
00:38:00,010 --> 00:38:01,270
I have to bring this up.

496
00:38:02,010 --> 00:38:02,990
What is it?

497
00:38:08,950 --> 00:38:10,750
I think Lin Zhixia needs a phone.

498
00:38:17,590 --> 00:38:18,510
Because she is a girl,

499
00:38:18,510 --> 00:38:19,400
it's not safe for her to be out alone.

500
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:20,480
So she needs a phone.

501
00:38:20,480 --> 00:38:21,800
All her classmates have phones too.

502
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:22,920
She looks out of place without one.

503
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:24,580
Therefore, she needs a phone.

504
00:38:34,670 --> 00:38:35,590
Oh, about that.

505
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:36,590
Actually,

506
00:38:36,590 --> 00:38:39,320
your mom and I
have already discussed this.

507
00:38:39,440 --> 00:38:40,840
The New Year is coming soon.

508
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:42,150
Recently, the supermarket

509
00:38:42,150 --> 00:38:43,670
has stocked up on New Year goods.

510
00:38:43,670 --> 00:38:46,190
We were planning to buy you

511
00:38:46,510 --> 00:38:47,960
each a phone after

512
00:38:47,980 --> 00:38:49,150
the New Year.

513
00:38:49,150 --> 00:38:49,760
Yes.

514
00:38:50,880 --> 00:38:52,710
Dad, I don't need a phone right now.

515
00:38:52,710 --> 00:38:54,920
But please get one for Lin Zhixia first.

516
00:38:55,030 --> 00:38:56,560
And the sooner, the better.

517
00:39:26,100 --> 00:39:30,850
[The 6th Nanhai Provincial Symposium
on Marine Science Development]

518
00:39:33,910 --> 00:39:36,350
[The 6th Nanhai Provincial Symposium
on Marine Science Development]

519
00:39:39,710 --> 00:39:41,360
Why is it so blurry?

520
00:39:47,050 --> 00:39:48,250
It's all out of focus.

521
00:40:09,840 --> 00:40:12,030
Should we retake...
